  "query_preview": "..(This Afternoon Through Friday)\nIssued at 1106 AM MDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nUpper level ridge will remain anchored over the Rockies into the \nPlains supporting hot temperatures. Very hot temps the next two \ndays as the core of the thermal ridge passes over the region. \nExpect temps into the 100s on most of the SD Plains and portions \nof the WY Plains. Heat products look good most areas, did expand \nthe extreme heat warning west a couple zones given hotter than \nexpected temps, with heat index readings of 105 to 110 expected \nthere. A stronger shortwave filled with monsoon moisture will \nadvect around the ridge in SW flow and across the FA today, \nsupporting high based TS. Damaging winds will be possible with \nthunderstorms given very high based nature and resultant \ninverted-V profiles per drying BL. Sct wind gusts over 60 mph \n(possibly over 80 mph in stronger cells) will be possible given \nDCAPE over 2000 J/KG, esp on the SD Plains east of the Black \nHills. Not much rain expected with these cells, which will support\ncritical fire weather conds when coupled with dry fuels, \ndownburst winds, and low RH. Things will dry out tonight, but it \nwill remain very warm with lows in the 70s at many areas, with 80s\nin the BH foothills. Another hot day Sunday with dry conds most \nareas. The exception will be over the BH where diurnal convection \nwill be possible and with another impulse toward the evening and \novernight. Convection will be possible with this wave mainly in \nthe western third. Expect gusty winds once again. Ridge will \nretrograde back west some by mid next week, supporting slightly \ncooler but still hot temps as highs in the 90s are expected. \nIsold-sct TS chances will continue as the lee trough interacts \nwill passing impulses. Main threat from storms will be strong \ngusty winds given high LCL's and inverted V profiles.",
